HT AWARDED $40 MILLION FIVE-YEAR CONTRACT BY AIR FORCE SUSTAINMENT CENTER AT ROBINS AIR FORCE BASE, GEORGIA'}{'symbol': 'KLAC', 'date': '2021-05-06 14:02:00', 'title': 'KLA FOUNDATION PLEDGES $550,000 TO COVID-19 RELIEF IN INDIA', 'text': "MILPITAS, CALIF., MAY 6, 2021 /PRNEWSWIRE/ -- KLA CORPORATION (NASDAQ: KLAC) TODAY\xa0ANNOUNCED THE KLA FOUNDATION IS EXPANDING ITS COVID-19 RELIEF EFFORTS IN INDIA WITH A DONATION OF $550,000 TO HELP COMBAT THE SECOND WAVE OF CORONAVIRUS INFECTIONS CURRENTLY TAXING THE COUNTRY'S HEALTHCARE SYSTEM AMIDST A NATIONAL VACCINE SHORTAGE."}{'symbol': 'LDOS', 'date': '2021-05-06 08:00:00', 'title': 'LEIDOS AWARDED SPOT ON $12.6 BILLION DIA SITE III IT SUPPORT CONTRACT', 'text': "RESTON, VA., MAY 6, 2021 /PRNEWSWIRE/ --\xa0LEIDOS (NYSE:LDOS), A FORTUNE®\xa0500 SCIENCE AND TECHNOLOGY LEADER, WAS RECENTLY NAMED AS AN AWARDEE FOR THE DEFENSE INTELLIGENCE AGENCY'S (DIA) SOLUTIONS FOR THE INFORMATION TECHNOLOGY ENTERPRISE III (SITE III) CONTRACT VEHICLE."}{'symbol': 'LLY', 'date': '2021-05-06 06:45:00', 'title': 'LILLY COLLABORATES INTERNATIONALLY WITH LEADING DIABETES TECHNOLOGY COMPANIES TO INTEGRATE CONNECTED INSULIN PEN SOLUTIONS FOR PEOPLE WITH DIABETES', 'text': "INDIANAPOLIS, MAY 6, 2021 /PRNEWSWIRE/ --\xa0WITH A GOAL OF INTEGRATING DATA AND TECHNOLOGY TO HELP STREAMLINE DIABETES MANAGEMENT, ELI LILLY AND COMPANY (NYSE: LLY) SIGNED STRATEGIC INTERNATIONAL AGREEMENTS WITH FOUR COMPANIES – DEXCOM, INC., GLOOKO INC., MYDIABBY HEALTHCARE AND ROCHE\xa0– TO ADVANCE CONNECTED SOLUTIONS AND STREAMLINE CARE FOR PEOPLE LIVING WITH DIABETES IN MARKETS OUTSIDE OF THE UNITED STATES. THESE COMPANIES OFFER UNIQUE DIABETES MANAGEMENT PLATFORMS THAT WILL BE COMPATIBLE WITH LILLY'S TEMPO PEN™ (APPROVED IN SEVERAL GLOBAL MARKETS) AND TEMPO SMART BUTTON™ (CURRENTLY IN LATE-STAGE DEVELOPMENT) TO SUPPORT PEOPLE WITH DIABETES AND HEALTHCARE PROFESSIONALS."}{'symbol': 'LIN', 'date': '2021-05-06 06:30:00', 'title': 'LINDE PLC: LINDE REPORTS FIRST-QUARTER 2021 R